{"name":"Fungal Hallucinations","hex":"#cc00dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fungal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to a fungus or fungi."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fungus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fungal"},{"term":"hallucinations","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of hallucination"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hallucinations"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fungus","blocks":[{"text":"A fungus is any member of the group of eukaryotic organisms that includes yeasts, molds, and mushrooms. These organisms are classified in the biological kingdom Fungi."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Fungi_collage.jpg/330px-Fungi_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fungus","wikidata":"Q764"},{"title":"Hallucination","blocks":[{"text":"A hallucination is a perception in the absence of an external context stimulus that has the compelling sense of reality. They are distinguishable from several related phenomena, such as dreaming, which does not involve wakefulness; pseudohallucination, which does not mimic real perception, and is accurately perceived as unreal; illusion, which involves distorted or misinterpreted real perception; and mental imagery, which does not mimic real perception, and is under voluntary control. Hallucinations also differ from \"delusional perceptions\", in which a correctly sensed and interpreted stimulus is given some additional significance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/August_Natterer_Meine_Augen_zur_Zeit_der_Erscheinungen.jpg/330px-August_Natterer_Meine_Augen_zur_Zeit_der_Erscheinungen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallucination","wikidata":"Q130741"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.o